# installd stats every mounted filesystem to decide which ones support quotas
# (InstalldNativeService::invalidateMounts -> GetQuotaProjectId). Three of this
# device's context= mounts are vendor types it has no rule for:
#
#   avc: denied { quotaget } for comm="binder:2486_1" scontext=u:r:installd:s0
#        tcontext=u:object_r:firmware_file:s0     tclass=filesystem
#        tcontext=u:object_r:bt_firmware_file:s0
#        tcontext=u:object_r:fsg_file:s0
#
# 15 per boot (5 mounts x 3 types). These are /vendor/firmware_mnt,
# /vendor/bt_firmware and /vendor/fsg -- read-only ext4 images mounted with
# context=, none of which support project quotas anyway.
#
# COSMETIC: installd treats the failure as "no quota support", which is the
# correct answer for these mounts. The grant only stops it asking noisily.
# quotaget is a filesystem-class permission; it conveys nothing but the
# quotactl(Q_GETQUOTA) result and no file access.
allow installd { firmware_file bt_firmware_file fsg_file }:filesystem quotaget;
